# The repository guard runs from the proposed pull-request tree, so the tree that
# can weaken it is the tree under review. Requiring Code Owner review on these
# paths is what keeps that from being a self-approval.
#
# The package manifests are here because they declare the commands CI runs, at
# both levels: the root scripts, and the menu and website `check`, `lint`, and
# `test` entries that `check:project` dispatches. Without them a pull request
# could replace a real check with `true` and watch project-ci go green. The
# guard jobs additionally invoke their scripts directly, so they do not depend
# on a script name staying honest either.
/.github/ @kiaquila
/docs/standards/ @kiaquila
/package.json @kiaquila
/menu/package.json @kiaquila
/website/package.json @kiaquila
/scripts/ @kiaquila
/tests/ @kiaquila
